Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Reading the Record: Analysis, Inference, and Feedback in Continuous Quantum \
Measurement\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A computation-first sequel to ",
 StyleBox["Watching a Qubit", "TI"],
 ". We keep exactly the same readout map ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalR]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 " and positivity-preserving trajectory map ",
 Cell[BoxData["\|01d4af"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 ", then ask what can be learned or controlled from the numbers a detector \
actually returns. Built-in Wolfram Language functions expose correlations, \
spectra, and changing frequencies; the same conditional update reconstructs a \
state from an external record; a likelihood turns innovations into parameter \
estimates; and record feedback closes the loop. The Function Repository's ",
 Cell[BoxData["LindbladSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 " supplies independent master-equation references, exactly as it did in the \
companion chapter."
}], "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami. Last updated July 31, 2026.", "Author",ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["Setting the Stage: From a Trajectory to a Data Analysis", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The companion chapter, ",
 StyleBox["Watching a Qubit: Continuous Measurement and Quantum Trajectories",
   "TI"],
 ", built two objects. The readout map ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalR]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " produces one vector of detector increments, and the trajectory map ",
 Cell[BoxData["\|01d4af"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 " uses those increments to propagate the conditional state. That chapter \
used the record mainly to explain where a trajectory comes from. Here the \
record becomes the main object of study."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The distinction to hold onto is simple: the detector returns increments ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 ", not a density matrix. The current ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 " is a rescaled view of the same data. A conditional state, a spectral peak, \
a parameter estimate, and a feedback command are all computations made from \
that stream."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell["\<\
In other words, there is one raw object and several questions we can ask of \
it:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["Question", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
     Cell["Record calculation", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
     Cell["What it can tell us", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"]},
   {Cell["Does the record remember its past?", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "CorrelationFunction"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"], Cell[
    "Oscillation and decay scales", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"]},
   {Cell["Which frequencies persist?", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData["PeriodogramArray"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
     " or ",
     Cell[BoxData["PowerSpectralDensity"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"], 
    Cell["Resonances and noise floor", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"]},
   {Cell["Does the frequency change with time?", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "SpectrogramArray"], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"], Cell[
    "Nonstationary dynamics", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"]},
   {Cell["What state is consistent with the readings?", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"], Cell[TextData[{
     "The conditional update inside ",
     Cell[BoxData["\|01d4af"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"], 
    Cell["Filtered state", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"]},
   {Cell["Which model best predicts the readings?", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData["LogLikelihood"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
     " of the innovations"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"], 
    Cell["Parameter estimate", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"]},
   {Cell["Can the readings steer the system?", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"], Cell[
    "Measurement followed by a record-dependent unitary", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"], Cell[
    "Feedback control", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
  GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {
      Scaled[0.14], 
      Scaled[0.37], 
      Scaled[0.37]}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
  GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.5}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}]], "Text",Express\
ionUUID->"2f1a5393-bc07-4c14-b1be-dd7946f2bd3a"],

Cell["\<\
I strongly believe in a computation-first narrative for learning: in a sense, \
if I cannot compute it, I cannot claim to understand it. Each section \
therefore makes one physical claim, computes it, and checks it against either \
synthetic shot noise, a replay of the same record, or an independent \
master-equation calculation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],

Cell["\<\
This is a live Wolfram notebook. Evaluate it from top to bottom in a fresh \
kernel because later cells depend on earlier ones. The narrative is a \
continuous sequence, like a movie: read each output and its physical meaning \
before studying every detail of the input. You are not locked into the \
baseline parameters. Once the notebook runs, change the drive, rate, step, \
record length, and random seed, then ask which conclusions survive. Questions \
and corrections are welcome through the repository that contains this lesson.\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell["Prerequisites and How to Read This", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The prerequisites are the companion chapter, basic density matrices, and \
the distinction between a Wiener increment of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 " and a current sample of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 ". We use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],
 " throughout. The pace steepens in the likelihood and feedback parts, but \
each new layer still begins from the same two maps. The long-record cells \
take more time than the short examples because frequency resolution is bought \
with observation time. My suggestion is to focus on what each output \
establishes before worrying about every implementation detail."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The code uses plain complex matrices and built-in Wolfram Language \
functions. Like the companion chapter, it calls ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"ResourceFunction", "[", "\"\<LindbladSolve\>\"", "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 " for deterministic master-equation references. The resource installs \
automatically on first use, so that first evaluation may need a network \
connection."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],

Cell["Part I: Preserve the Record Contract", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell["\<\
The source of truth is the companion chapter. Its readout convention is\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["y", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "=", 
    SqrtBox[
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], " ", 
    StyleBox["Tr",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "+", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]}], "\[Tilde]", 
    RowBox[{"\|01d4a9", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        StyleBox[
         RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalR]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],
 " returns one increment per monitored channel, while ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[ScriptCapitalT]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 " returns the list of conditional states and ",
 Cell[BoxData["Sow"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 "s those increments as a side effect."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell["\<\
Copy the two definitions without refactoring them so this notebook and the \
companion cannot silently adopt different update rules:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalR]", ",", " ", "\[ScriptCapitalT]"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalR]", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "\[Rho]_", ",", " ", "Ls_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "dw_", ",", " ", 
      "\[Eta]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "#3", "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"#1", " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#1", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", ".",
            " ", "\[Rho]"}], "]"}], " ", "dt"}], " ", "+", " ", "#2"}], " ", 
       "&"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"Ls", ",", " ", "dw", ",", " ", "\[Eta]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
   ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[Rho]0_", "?", "MatrixQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"H_", "?", "MatrixQ"}], ",", " ", "Ls_List", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"None", " ", "|", " ", "_List"}], ")"}], " ", ":", " ", 
      "None"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"V", " ", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"None", " ", "|", " ", "_List"}], ")"}], " ", ":", " ", 
      "None"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tf_", "?", "NumericQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Length", "[", "\[Rho]0", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"r0", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"N", "[", "\[Rho]0", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Hn", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"N", "[", "H", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Lsn", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"N", "[", "Ls", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"dtn", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"N", "[", "dt", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", "\[Eta]v", ",", 
       " ", "Vsn", ",", " ", "heff", ",", " ", "lcorr", ",", " ", "nsteps", ",",
        " ", "dw", ",", " ", "step"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Eta]v", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"N", "[", 
        RowBox[{"If", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "===", " ", "None"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Length", "[", "Ls", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\[Eta]"}],
          "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Vsn", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"If", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"V", " ", "===", " ", "None"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"N", "[", "V", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"heff", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "d", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dtn", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"I", " ", "Hn"}], "\n", "       ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
                "#"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "Lsn"}], "]"}]}], "\n", 
           "       ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
                "#"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "Vsn"}], "]"}]}]}], 
          ")"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"lcorr", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"dtn", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
         RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"#1", " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"#2", " ", ".", " ", "#2"}], ")"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"\[Eta]v", ",", " ", "Lsn"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";",
       "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"nsteps", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
        RowBox[{"tf", "/", "dt"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"dw", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dtn", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Length", "[", "Lsn", "]"}], ",", " ", "nsteps"}], 
           "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"step", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]_", ",", " ", "dwv_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"dy", ",", " ", "s", ",", " ", "m", ",", " ", "num"}], 
          "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"dy", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sow", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalR]", "[", 
             RowBox[{
             "\[Rho]", ",", " ", "Lsn", ",", " ", "dtn", ",", " ", "dwv", ",",
               " ", "\[Eta]v"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
            RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"#1", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "#2", "]"}], " ", "#3"}], " ", "&"}], ",",
               " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"dy", ",", " ", "\[Eta]v", ",", " ", "Lsn"}], "}"}]}], 
             "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"heff", " ", "+", " ", "s", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"s", " ", ".", " ", "s"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "lcorr"}]}], 
          ";", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"num", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"m", " ", ".", " ", "\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", 
             RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "m", "]"}]}], "\n", 
            "          ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"dtn", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{"#", " ", ".", " ", "\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ",
                 "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "Vsn"}], "]"}]}], "\n", "          ", 
            "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"dtn", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
              RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ")"}], " ", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{"#1", " ", ".", " ", "\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#1", "]"}]}], ")"}]}],
                  " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"Lsn", ",", " ", "\[Eta]v"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
              "]"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"num", "/", 
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "num", "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
       RowBox[{"step", ",", " ", "r0", ",", " ", "dw"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],

Cell["\<\
This is the one deliberately dense cell in the lesson. It is infrastructure \
copied from the companion, not a new idea compressed into code.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now choose the same matrix conventions as the companion. The lowering \
operator sends the excited basis vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],
 " to the ground basis vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"X", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Y", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Z", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Jminus", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"X", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", "Y"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Jminus", " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Jminus", " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[2]= ",ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
A state vector still needs to become a density matrix. Define that \
conversion, a Bloch-vector reader, and one reusable density-operator test \
explicitly:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "densityMatrix", ",", " ", "blochVector", ",", " ", "densityOperatorQ"}], 
   "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "\[Psi]", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "\[Rho]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"X", ",", " ", "Y", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"densityOperatorQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Rho]_", "?", "MatrixQ"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Abs", "@", 
       RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "\[Rho]", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}],
      " ", "<", " ", 
     RowBox[{"10", "^", 
      RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}]}], " ", "&&", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "\[Rho]", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}], " ", "<",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"10", "^", 
      RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}]}], " ", "&&", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
       RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"\[Rho]", " ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "\[Rho]", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
         "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", ">", " ", 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      RowBox[{"10", "^", 
       RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}]}]}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell["\<\
We need a long, approximately stationary record. Drive an emitting qubit on \
resonance and let the transient occupy only a small fraction of the run:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]0", " ", "=", " ", "3.5"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]0", " ", "=", " ", "0.7"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"dt0", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tf0", " ", "=", " ", "1200."}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"H0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]0", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Y", "/", "2"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"L0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]0", "]"}], " ", "Jminus"}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"HermitianMatrixQ", "[", "H0", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"densityOperatorQ", "[", "\[Rho]0", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[4]= ",ExpressionUUID->"2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The two checks confirm that the numerical experiment starts from a Hermitian \
Hamiltonian and a Hermitian, unit-trace, positive state.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],

Cell["\<\
Generate the conditional states and reap the readout increments:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"trajectory0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "record0", "}"}]}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "1", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Reap", "@", 
      RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalT]", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Rho]0", ",", " ", "H0", ",", " ", "L0", ",", " ", "dt0", ",", " ", 
        "tf0"}], "]"}]}]}], "\n", "   ", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],

Cell["\<\
There is one monitored channel, so pull out its increments and build the \
corresponding current:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dy0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"record0", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"current0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dy0", "/", "dt0"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],

Cell["Check the scale before analyzing anything:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<samples\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Length", "[", "dy0", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<increment standard deviation\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "dy0", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Wiener scale\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dt0", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<current standard deviation\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "current0", "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"samples\"\>", "\[Rule]", "120000"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"increment standard deviation\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    "0.10001657309073447`"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Wiener scale\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.1`"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"current standard deviation\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    "10.001657309073446`"}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[7]= ",ExpressionUUID->"14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The increment fluctuates on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 " scale, while the current fluctuates on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],
 " scale. This is the first guardrail: filtering and likelihood consume ",
 Cell[BoxData["dy0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 "; a spectrum may use either ",
 Cell[BoxData["dy0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData["current0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 ", but its normalization must say which one it uses."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell["Part II: Correlation Before Spectrum", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A correlation asks whether two samples separated by a lag tend to move \
together. The built-in ",
 Cell[BoxData["CorrelationFunction"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 " subtracts the sample mean and normalizes by the variance, so it reports a \
dimensionless autocorrelation rather than the raw covariance."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell["\<\
In other words, the zero-lag shot-noise spike is scaled to one, and coherent \
dynamics appear as much smaller oscillations at nonzero lag.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the correlation from one step out to eight time units, skipping every \
fourth lag to keep the plot light:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lagSteps", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
      RowBox[{"8", "/", "dt0"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"corr0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"CorrelationFunction", "[", 
    RowBox[{"dy0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"First", "[", "lagSteps", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Last", "[", "lagSteps", "]"}], ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell["Plot it against physical lag rather than sample number:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"dt0", " ", "lagSteps"}], ",", " ", "corr0"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "560"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<lag \[Tau]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<normalized correlation\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<The raw record remembers the driven qubit at nonzero \
lag\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],

